# jsPDF's .save() can write a real file to the working directory when run
# under Node/jsdom in tests (rather than triggering a browser download) —
# safety net so test-generated PDFs never get committed again.
/*.pdf

# Agent worktrees and local CI experiments — never commit
New Folder With Items/.claude/
# .github/ WAS ignored here from 2026-07-05 until 2026-08-01, and it took the
# real CI config with it. ci.yml describes itself as a gate that means "a
# detection regression physically cannot reach main unnoticed" — it had never
# run once, because it was never committed. The apply worker's workflow hit the
# same trap: `git add -A` reported success and silently skipped it, so a commit
# whose message announced the worker's host shipped everything EXCEPT the host.
#
# Ignoring a whole directory to exclude experiments inside it is the mistake.
# If a local CI experiment needs excluding, name the file.
scripts/.prerender-data-entry.ts
scripts/.prerender-data.mjs
worker/applicant.json
worker/submit-*.png
